WEBVTT

00:00:00.425 --> 00:00:02.604
In this video, you will bring in help.

00:00:02.604 --> 00:00:08.804
You will add co-organizers, who share the work of running the contest, and judges, who score the homes.

00:00:08.804 --> 00:00:09.762
We start on the map.

00:00:10.743 --> 00:00:12.417
Start at SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:15.574 --> 00:00:18.124
On the home page, tap Use my location.

00:00:20.815 --> 00:00:21.795
Then tap Allow.

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:30.830
Now look at the top of the map, beside the search box.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:33.610
See your picture, or your initial, in a circle?

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:38.173
That is your account menu, and it is the doorway to everything else on the site.

00:00:38.173 --> 00:00:38.877
Tap it.

00:00:41.024 --> 00:00:42.987
In the menu, tap Your contests.

00:00:44.806 --> 00:00:48.901
That is where the contests you run, and the homes you entered, live.

00:00:48.901 --> 00:00:49.758
Tap Mine.

00:00:51.651 --> 00:00:53.621
This is your personal page.

00:00:53.621 --> 00:00:59.094
It lists the contests you run, if you run any, and the homes you entered, with their status.

00:00:59.094 --> 00:01:01.203
Tap Manage, next to your contest.

00:01:02.972 --> 00:01:07.081
This opens your dashboard, the control room for your contest.

00:01:07.081 --> 00:01:09.310
Running a contest is easier with help.

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:10.123
Tap Team.

00:01:11.787 --> 00:01:19.232
Co-organizers sign in and see your dashboard, so they can approve entries, review votes, and manage judges and sponsors.

00:01:19.232 --> 00:01:25.848
Only you, the creator, can change the contest details, pause voting, unpublish, or announce the winners.

00:01:26.675 --> 00:01:30.977
Only the creator can add co-organizers, and you can add up to eight.

00:01:30.977 --> 00:01:34.326
Type their email address, and tap Add co-organizer.

00:01:36.695 --> 00:01:41.051
They get an email like this one, with one button that opens the dashboard.

00:01:41.051 --> 00:01:44.539
They sign in with that same email address, and they are in.

00:01:45.488 --> 00:01:48.151
Judges are different from co-organizers.

00:01:48.151 --> 00:01:51.637
They score the homes, but they do not manage the contest.

00:01:51.637 --> 00:01:54.744
They are added on the Judges tab, so tap Judges.

00:01:56.448 --> 00:01:59.493
Type a judge's email address, and tap Add judge.

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:08.933
You can see who has signed in, and how many homes each judge has scored, so you know the judging is on track.

00:02:09.902 --> 00:02:12.905
Your judge gets an invitation like this one.

00:02:12.905 --> 00:02:19.040
It says which contest it is, how judging works, and has a button that opens their private ballot.

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:20.269
Nothing else to set up.

00:02:21.351 --> 00:02:23.011
Next up: Announce winners.
